## Why This Is Asked
Schema evolution and idempotent data ingestion are common in production; this tests how a candidate plans versioning, backward compatibility, and basic testing.

## Key Concepts
- GCS event-driven ingestion
- Cloud Functions and BigQuery inserts with insertId
- Versioned schemas in Cloud Storage
- Dead-lettering for invalid data
- Lightweight migration path for future versions

## Code Example
```javascript
const Ajv = require('ajv');
const {Storage} = require('@google-cloud/storage');
const storage = new Storage();
async function validateEvent(eventsBlob, version){
  const schemaObj = await fetchSchema(version);
  const validate = ajv.compile(schemaObj);
  const events = JSON.parse(await eventsBlob.downloadBuffer());
  return events.every(e => validate(e));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle migrating existing data when adding v2?
- How would you test this with large payloads and schema drift?

